es where we don't have to  kind of push all the artifacts around  but the experience is exactly the same  so so now I'm just going to go and  change some code here I'm gonna say  hello coop con and then I just saved it  and this will read this will kick off  the kind of build and deploy cycle again  and you can see that we've already  redeployed our new pod and it's printing  out hello coop cons so you get that  really kind of fast inner development  loop of  for for your work that was incredibly  incredibly fast it's so of course you  know this is a minimal example so we're  only deploying a very small go binary  but in practice it is it is quite fast  and have you heard from users using  scaffold for much larger maybe real  production type workloads yeah  absolutely and in that case you know  it's still great for that kind of inner  development loop but we also have a mode  called scaffold run and so scaffold run  will just run this build and deploy  pipeline one so the idea is that you can  you can call this from you know a  product such as Google container builder  or you know Jenkins or spinnaker and  then you can kind of have the same kind  of see ICD workflow as you have locally  so that kind of bridges the gap and  users aren't left on this cliff of  having all of these tools locally and  then having to relearn something else in  their see ICD pipelines that's superb

